      "content": {
        "text": {
          "paragraphs": [
            "康托(G. Cantor, 1845—1918)，德国数学家，集合论创始人。"
          ]
        },
        "table": null,
        "equation": null,
        "figure": null
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "p9_h1",
      "kind": "text",
      "zone": "main",
      "role": "figure_caption",
      "bbox": [
        350,
        130,
        670,
        170
      ],
      "anchor_id": null,
      "figure_group_id": null,
      "content": {
        "text": {
          "paragraphs": [
            "1.1 集合初步"
          ]
        },
        "table": null,
        "equation": null,
        "figure": null
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "p9_h2",
      "kind": "text",
      "zone": "main",
      "role": "figure_caption",
      "bbox": [
        350,
        230,
        470,
        270
      ],
      "anchor_id": null,
      "figure_group_id": null,
      "content": {
        "text": {
          "paragraphs": [
            "1 集合"
          ]
        },
        "table": null,
        "equation": null,
        "figure": null
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "p9_b1",
      "kind": "text",
      "zone": "main",
      "role": "example",
      "bbox": [
        330,
        300,
        910,
        460
      ],
      "anchor_id": null,
      "figure_group_id": null,
      "content": {
        "text": {
          "paragraphs": [
            "我们经常需要把满足一定要求或具有一定特征的对象放在一起或归为一类. 例如：",
            "(1) 申辉中学高一(1)班的全体学生；",
            "(2) 所有不大于 $100$ 的自然数；",
            "(3) 直线 $l$ 上的所有点；",
            "(4) 不等式 $2x+1 \\leqslant 0$ 的所有解；",
            "(5) 太阳系的所有行星."
          ]
        },
        "table": null,
        "equation": null,
        "figure": null
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "p9_b2",
      "kind": "text",
      "zone": "main",
      "role": "example",
      "bbox": [
        330,
        460,
        910,
        495
      ],
      "anchor_id": null,
      "figure_group_id": null,
      "content": {
        "text": {
          "paragraphs": [
            "概括地说，把一些确定的对象的全体叫做集合(set)，简称集. 集合通常用大写字母 $A$、$B$、$C$……表示."
          ]
        },
        "table": null,
        "equation": null,
        "figure": null
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "p9_b3",
      "kind": "text",
      "zone": "main",
      "role": "example",
      "bbox": [
        330,
        495,
        910,
        540
      ],
      "anchor_id": null,
      "figure_group_id": null,
      "content": {
        "text": {
          "paragraphs": [
            "集合所含的各个对象叫做该集合的元素(element). 元素通常用小写字母 $a$、$b$、$c$……表示."
          ]
        },
        "table": null,
        "equation": null,
        "figure": null
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "p9_b4",
      "kind": "text",
      "zone": "main",
      "role": "example",
      "bbox": [
        330,
        540,
        910,
        605
      ],
      "anchor_id": null,
      "figure_group_id": null,
      "content": {
        "text": {
          "paragraphs": [
            "如果 $a$ 是集合 $A$ 的元素，就记作 $a \\in A$，读作“$a$ 属于 $A$”；如果 $a$ 不是集合 $A$ 的元素，就记作 $a \\notin A$，读作“$a$ 不属于 $A$”. 例如，若 $A$ 是由数 $1$、$3$、$5$、$7$、$9$ 组成的集合，则 $1 \\in A$，$2 \\notin A$."
          ]
        },
        "table": null,
        "equation": null,
        "figure": null
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "p9_b5",
      "kind": "text",
      "zone": "main",
      "role": "example",
      "bbox": [
        330,
        605,
        910,
        695
      ],
      "anchor_id": null,
      "figure_group_id": null,
      "content": {
        "text": {
          "paragraphs": [
            "集合的元素是确定的. 也就是说，给定一个集合，一个对象在不在这个集合中就确定了. 例如，“我国的直辖市”组成一个集合，北京、上海、天津、重庆在这个集合中，而杭州、南京、深圳等城市不在这个集合中."
          ]
        },
        "table": null,
        "equation": null,
        "figure": null
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "p9_b6",
      "kind": "text",
      "zone": "main",
      "role": "example",
      "bbox": [
        330,
        695,
        910,
        755
      ],
      "anchor_id": null,
      "figure_group_id": null,
      "content": {
        "text": {
          "paragraphs": [
            "一些不确定的对象不能组成一个集合. 例如，“我们班里高个子的同学”不能组成一个集合. 因为“高个子”的标准不够明确、具体，所以“我们班里高个子的同学”是不确定的."
          ]
        },
        "table": null,
        "equation": null,
        "figure": null
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "p9_b7",
      "kind": "text",
      "zone": "main",
      "role": "example",
      "bbox": [
        330,
        755,
        910,
        805
      ],
      "anchor_id": null,
      "figure_group_id": null,
      "content": {
        "text": {
          "paragraphs": [
            "一个给定集合中的各个元素是互不相同的，即一个元素在同一个集合中是不能重复出现的."
          ]
        },
        "table": null,
        "equation": null,
        "figure": null
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "p9_b8",
      "kind": "text",
      "zone": "main",
      "role": "example",
      "bbox": [
        330,
        805,
        910,
        845
      ],
      "anchor_id": null,
      "figure_group_id": null,
      "content": {
        "text": {
          "paragraphs": [
            "如果两个集合 $A$ 与 $B$ 的组成元素完全相同，就称这两个集合相等，记作 $A=B$."
          ]
        },
        "table": null,
        "equation": null,
        "figure": null
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "p9_b9",
      "kind": "text",
      "zone": "main",
      "role": "example",
      "bbox": [
        330,
        845,
        910,
        870
      ],
      "anchor_id": null,
      "figure_group_id": null,
      "content": {
        "text": {
          "paragraphs": [
            "元素个数有限的集合称为有限集，否则就称为无限集."
          ]
        },
        "table": null,
        "equation": null,
        "figure": null
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "p9_b10",
      "kind": "text",
      "zone": "main",
      "role": "example",
      "bbox": [
        330,
        870,
        910,
        920
      ],
      "anchor_id": null,
      "figure_group_id": null,
      "content": {
        "text": {
          "paragraphs": [
            "例 1 判断下列集合是有限集还是无限集，并说明理由：",
            "(1) $6$ 的正整数倍的全体组成的集合；"
          ]
        },
        "table": null,
        "equation": null,
        "figure": null
      }
    },
